# Answer 12 · The Multidisciplinary Nature of Gender Studies (CSS 2022)
@py question 2022-2

## The answer map
::: fig mindmap | The answer map: every branch is one numbered heading of the model answer below.
@note "In detail": define the terms, explain why the field uses many disciplines, then one heading per discipline with a thinker and a Pakistani example.
@ask DISCUSS IN DETAIL the MULTIDISCIPLINARY NATURE of Gender Studies
(1) Introduction: GS studies gender with many disciplines; multi, inter and trans explained
(2) Why many disciplines: gender is everywhere; problems are complex; founders came from many subjects
(3) Sociology: roles are made by society; Oakley on housework
(4) Anthropology: gender differs by culture; Mead, Ortner
(5) Psychology: identity and stereotypes; Bem, Gilligan
(6) History: finding women's past; Lerner on patriarchy's origin
(7) Economics: unpaid work and development; Boserup, Waring
(8) Politics and law: power and rights; Pateman, MacKinnon, CEDAW
(9) Biology and medicine: sex, intersex, women's health
(10) Literature, language, media: women writers; biased words; male gaze
(11) Development and religion: WID to GAD; re-reading holy texts
(12) Strengths and weaknesses: full picture vs no clear home
(13) Conclusion: many voices, one conversation
